---
import PuzzleFrame from '../../components/PuzzleFrame.astro';
import concepts from '../../data/puzzle-concepts.json';
const businessHub = Object.keys(import.meta.glob('../ues/business.astro')).length ? '/ues/business' : '/ues';
const modules=[
 ['Read the table','Choose one audience, one occasion and one comfortable challenge. Compare three physical puzzles for piece size, contrast, grip and reference readability. A desk study can use specifications; label what has not been physically examined.','A one-page audience brief with three access hypotheses.','How do you know this is a need rather than your preference?'],
 ['Compose a solve','Mark obvious anchors, edge clues, texture regions and deliberate hard areas. Make a grayscale check so landmarks do not depend only on hue. Try three crops and explain which gives the most useful clues.','A color-and-shape zone map plus three annotated crops.','Does each part of the image give someone a place to begin?'],
 ['Turn art into an object','Select a tentative piece count and print size. Calculate effective pixels per inch, inspect details at actual piece scale and follow one supplier template. Draw the box, insert and opening sequence.','A supplier-specific specification, piece-scale proof sheet and packaging sketch.','What must be proven physically rather than assumed from the screen?'],
 ['Test with care','Plan a voluntary adult playtest with consent, varied experience and optional hints. Ask about comfort, landmarks, false fits and reference use. Do not collect diagnoses or publish names. Do not invent completed findings.','An unrun test protocol, or an anonymous observation report if a real test happens.','Can someone contribute without racing, seeing every color or handling tiny pieces?'],
 ['Cost the promise','Use the business lab to compare a pilot, direct retail and wholesale. Replace assumptions with dated quotes where available. Track packaging, labor, postage, replacements and acquisition.','A contribution worksheet, cash-timing diagram and three stress cases.','Can the product survive higher costs or half the expected demand?'],
 ['Make a responsible brief','Write an honest pitch: picture, audience, specification, proof evidence, rights, costs and unresolved questions. Distinguish proposed work from tested results. Prepare an IndustryNext-style case narrative with clear sources.','A five-page launch dossier and a pass, revise or stop decision.','Which claim would you remove because the evidence is not yet there?']
];
const fields=[['Audience and occasion','Who is this for, and why would they choose it?'],['Image and solving plan','Name the landmarks, difficult zones and proposed piece count.'],['Access and physical proof','What will you test for lighting, grip, contrast and reference use?'],['Rights and supplier evidence','Record permissions, human edits, specification, quote date and exclusions.'],['Business and cash','Use contribution, fixed work, inventory cash and downside cases.'],['Next decision','What would make you proceed, revise or stop?']];
---
<PuzzleFrame title="The puzzle design studio" description="Six open puzzle design and business modules, ten original concept briefs, a private downloadable worksheet and links to UES and Industry Next education." active="studio">
  <header class="p-hero"><div class="p-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">UNIVERSITY OF EL SEGUNDO · OPEN DESIGN & BUSINESS CASE</p><h1>Design<br/>the solve.</h1><p class="p-lead">The picture is one design problem. The piece, the table, the box and the business are four more.</p><p>Six self-directed modules connect visual practice to manufacturing and business. Work privately, at your pace. There is no application, grade submission or purchase required.</p><div class="p-actions"><a class="p-button" href="#modules">Start the studio ↓</a><a class="p-button secondary" href="#worksheet">Make a private brief</a></div></div><figure class="p-hero-art"><img src="/images/puzzles/06-small-wonders.webp" alt={concepts[5].alt} width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>06 / Workshop of small wonders · Original artwork study · Proposed puzzle</figcaption></figure></header>
  <div class="p-band">Independent, unaccredited educational project. A proposed puzzle case, with no claim of enrolled students, completed cohorts or commercial partnerships.</div>
  <section class="p-section" id="modules"><div class="p-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 · SIX MODULES</p><h2>Observe.<br/>Make. Test. Cost.</h2></div><p>Each module leaves a keepable artifact. A concept brief can be completed using this site and public sources; manufacturing and user testing remain optional future work.</p></div><div class="p-grid p-curriculum">{modules.map(m=><article class="p-card"><h3>{m[0]}</h3><p>{m[1]}</p><p><b>Deliver:</b> {m[2]}</p><p><b>Critique:</b> {m[3]}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="p-section" id="briefs"><div class="p-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 · TEN BRIEFS, TEN DIFFERENT QUESTIONS</p><h2>Choose your<br/>first study.</h2></div><p>The gallery’s proposed counts are starting hypotheses. Change the plan if composition, print tests or user observations give a reason.</p></div><div class="p-concepts">{concepts.map(c=><article class="p-card" id={`brief-${c.id}`}><p class="eyebrow">BRIEF {c.id} · {c.pieces.toLocaleString()} PROPOSED PIECES</p><h3>{c.title}</h3><p><b>Study:</b> {c.lesson}.</p><p>{c.challenge}</p><p><b>Physical test:</b> {c.print}</p><p><b>Business decision:</b> {c.pilot}</p><a href={`/puzzles/#concept-${c.slug}`}>Return to the artwork →</a></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="p-section" id="worksheet"><div class="p-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 · A PRIVATE DESIGN BRIEF</p><h2>Keep the<br/>questions together.</h2></div><p>Write locally in this page and download your own text file. Notes are not transmitted or saved automatically. Navigating away can lose them.</p></div><form id="p-worksheet"><div class="p-grid">{fields.map(([label,prompt],i)=><label>{label}<textarea name={`study-${i}`} rows="6" placeholder={prompt}></textarea></label>)}</div><div class="p-actions"><button id="p-download" type="button" class="p-button" disabled>Download my brief (.txt)</button><button type="reset" class="p-button secondary">Clear this page’s notes</button></div><p id="p-worksheet-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No notes are saved automatically.</p></form><noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to download the worksheet. You can also copy the six questions into your own notebook.</p></noscript></section>
  <section class="p-section"><div class="p-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 · THE CONNECTIONS</p><h2>A studio within<br/>a wider school.</h2></div><p>Use existing UES resources and the Industry Next Communications Lab as educational companions. These links describe editorial connections, not institutional partnerships.</p></div><div class="p-grid"><article class="p-card"><h3>Business concentration</h3><p>Demand, contribution, inventory and distribution are the business questions behind the design. Begin with the puzzle case, then compare another local operating model.</p><a href="/puzzles/business/">Open this business case →</a><p class="p-small" style="margin-top:12px"><a href={businessHub}>Explore UES business studies</a></p></article><article class="p-card"><h3>Public Image Office</h3><p>UES’s existing image-making studio provides a related home for visual language, public claims, attribution and image responsibility.</p><a href="/ues/public-image-office">Open UES-203 →</a></article><article class="p-card"><h3>Common Table</h3><p>UES’s existing community studio asks what a welcoming shared setting needs. Apply that lens to puzzle tables, references and participation.</p><a href="/ues/common-table">Open UES-206 →</a></article><article class="p-card"><h3>Industry Next case study</h3><p>Trace one design decision through image, cut, manufacturing and customer experience. The PointCast-hosted Communications Lab offers a verified public doorway for applied briefs.</p><a href="/communications-lab/">Open the Communications Lab →</a><p class="p-small" style="margin-top:14px"><a href="https://www.industrynext.xyz/make/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Industry Next Permission Lab ↗</a> — compare private drafting with deliberate publishing.</p><p class="p-small"><a href="https://www.industrynext.xyz/editorial/the-wild-one-cent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Case: One cent, remembered ↗</a> — distinguish a working mechanism from evidence of outside demand.</p></article><article class="p-card"><h3>El Segundo School archive</h3><p>Study the existing art archive as a visual resource. An archive link does not grant commercial reproduction rights to its artworks; follow each work’s rights record.</p><a href="/el-segundo-school">Explore the archive →</a></article><article class="p-card"><h3>Buildworks complement</h3><p>The companion Buildworks studio focuses on small crafted objects. This case focuses on puzzles. Compare material use, packaging and rights across formats without assuming a bundle will sell.</p><a href="/puzzles/#concept-small-wonders">Study the workshop puzzle →</a></article></div><p class="p-note" style="margin-top:25px">A useful critique asks for evidence: Is the image readable? Does the actual cut work? Can different people participate? Are rights and sources clear? Do the numbers withstand stress? What remains unknown?</p></section>
</PuzzleFrame>
<script>
  function setupPuzzleWorksheet(){const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#p-worksheet');if(!form||form.dataset.ready)return;form.dataset.ready='true';form.addEventListener('submit',e=>e.preventDefault());const download=form.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#p-download')!;download.disabled=false;download.addEventListener('click',()=>{const fields=Array.from(form.querySelectorAll<HTMLTextAreaElement>('textarea'));const text=['PointCast puzzle studio — private design brief',new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10),'Educational work; proposed choices require proof and review.','',...fields.flatMap(field=>[field.parentElement!.childNodes[0].textContent!.trim(),field.value||'[Not yet answered]',''])].join('\n');const url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([text],{type:'text/plain;charset=utf-8'}));const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='my-pointcast-puzzle-brief.txt';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);form.querySelector('#p-worksheet-status')!.textContent='Your brief was downloaded. Keep the file; this page does not save it.';});form.addEventListener('reset',()=>{form.querySelector('#p-worksheet-status')!.textContent='The page’s notes are cleared. Downloaded files are unchanged.';});}
  setupPuzzleWorksheet();document.addEventListener('astro:page-load',setupPuzzleWorksheet);
</script>
